	I have found a possible problem with lev_comp. In the
	course of playing with creating new .des files I discovered
	that I could not create a soldier, what I got was an oracle.
	I also checked by castle level and got oracles as well.
	I found that it was necessary to recompile lev_comp to correct
	this problem, because lev_comp uses pm.h to identify monsters
	and this file has changed from 3.0 to 3.0 pl6. It would appear
	that the files created for castle, endgame and tower are not
	portable across the patch levels. If pm.h changes this will
	cause the monster ids in the files to be outdated. The
	solution is to recompile lev_comp and recreate the castle
	endgame and tower files from the *.des files. This may
	have been part of a patch update which I missed (I'm on
	PL 6), if so....never mind...

	I would also suggest using the same names for things in
	lev_comp as in the rest of the game code. For example, 
	when I tried to create a "teleportation trap" the trap type
	was not recognized, "teleport" was needed instead. lev_comp
	has its own table with trap names and they are not the same
	as in trapname.h. 

	randy


